          },
          "description": "limit: the adaptive concurrency limit. It grows by one per success until the first failure (slow start), then by one per `limit` consecutive successes; failures and transient errors (5xx, 429, network) halve it at most once per 30s and pause growth for 60s. in flight: party setups currently running. retry queue: failed or resumed setups waiting to be retried. If in flight stays well below the limit, the allocator is not concurrency bound."
        }
      },
